==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|in|literacy}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈlɪtəɹəsi/|/ɪˈlɪt(ʃ)ɹəsi/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-illiteracy.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|illiteracies}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[inability]] to [[read]] and [[write]].
#: '''''Illiteracy''' is widespread in certain areas of the country.''
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The portion of a population unable to read and write, generally given as a percentage.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A word, phrase{{,}} or grammatical turn thought to be characteristic of an illiterate person.

